s=s[:at]+('The declaration cannot contain its own mandatory bytes/SHA or a self-referential fixed60-row table. It enumerates exactly the other59 proof paths and their fixed identities, plus non-self descriptive fields. The helper and producer contain the separately reviewed literal declaration identity; the collector pins the helper before import and also pins the same declaration in its independent12-role tooling table. Each reader forms the combined set from those59 rows plus the externally pinned declaration, then asserts exactly60 unique paths, exact row fingerprints and aggregate bounds. The declaration must not pin the helper/collector/producer that pins it. This mirrors the established externally pinned bundle boundary without an exception for arbitrary self identities, and creates no helper/collector/declaration/workflow hash cycle. A mutation of the declaration is rejected by those external fixed pins before its contents can define the other59 expectations.\n\n')+s[at:]
